        if(RP_FAM === ''){
          /* The board answered nothing usable. TWO DIFFERENT REASONS LIVE HERE
             and they used to share one sentence — which stated the harsher of
             the two as a fact about the adapter's SOFTWARE:

               * the routes are genuinely absent ("unknown route: …"), which is
                 what the sentence below describes, and every board the day
                 this shipped; or
               * the listing route exists and FAILED — a pairing file it could
                 not read, a 500, a token the proxy refused. That board may add
                 accounts perfectly well, and telling its owner the feature is
                 not built yet is simply false. It also left no way back: this
