             at all, because from here it is the same situation. */
          h += note('<b>Your adapter’s software cannot add accounts yet.</b> The part that links '+
                    'a PlayStation account is still being built, so there is nothing on this '+
                    'screen that could reach it.','warn')+
               note('Use the <b>ZeroStick dashboard on a PC</b> — its PlayStation panel runs the '+
                    'same sign-in and the same 8-digit pairing, straight onto the board.');
        } else if(!st.acct){
          if(!RP_MISSING.account){
            h += note('The quick way needs <b>no sign-in at all</b>. Your <b>PlayStation account '+
                      'ID</b> is a short code that identifies your PSN account — Chiaki-ng shows '+
                      'it, and so does any Chiaki or PS Play config you already have. Paste it '+
                      'here with a name you will recognise.')+
                 /* value= FROM MODULE STATE, for the reason the PIN is: every
                    press here ends in draw(), and data-nosave="1" means ZS.wire
