                        was the one being lost. The redirect URL carries a
                        single-use `code=` that Sony will not issue twice, so a
                        refusal that wiped the box — "that link did not carry a
                        working code", the one refusal it is actually FOR — sent
                        the user back through the whole sign-in for a fresh
                        link. It is held in memory only, never in the store, and
                        dropped the moment it is spent. */
                     card('<div class="fld col"><div class="flab">The address that page landed on</div>'+
                          '<input class="txt" id="psn-redir" data-nosave="1" style="margin-top:10px" '+
                          'inputmode="url" autocomplete="off" '+
                          'placeholder="https://remoteplay.dl.playstation.net/…?code=…" '+
                          'value="'+esc(st.redir)+'"></div>')+
